      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0011",
      "sequence": 866,
      "meaning": "At Suvela, Rāma descends with the immense army and finds a lofty, exceptionally lovely white peak. Lakṣmaṇa makes a bed of tender leaves and flowers, spreads a soft deerskin, and the compassionate Lord sits. Sugrīva’s head rests in his lap; bow and quiver lie to either side as he adjusts arrows in his lotus hands. Vibhīṣaṇa whispers counsel, Aṅgada and Hanumān massage his feet, and Lakṣmaṇa sits heroically behind with bow, arrow and quiver. Blessed are those absorbed in this image. Looking east, Rāma points out the fearless lionlike moon rising.",
