    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0013",
      "sequence": 868,
      "meaning": "Rāma points to what resembles storm-clouds, lightning and sweet thunder in the south. Vibhīṣaṇa explains that it is Rāvaṇa’s arena atop Laṅkā: his black parasol is the cloud, Mandodarī’s earrings are lightning, and the music is thunder. Smiling at the demon’s pride, Rāma strings his bow and shoots. One arrow strikes down the parasol, crown and earrings before all, though no one perceives the cause, then returns to Rāma’s quiver. Rāvaṇa’s assembly becomes fearful and its entertainment collapses.",
