    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0014",
      "sequence": 869,
      "meaning": "With no tremor, wind or visible weapon, everyone treats the fallen ornaments as a terrifying omen. Rāvaṇa laughs and dismisses it: heads constantly fall for the auspicious, so how can a fallen crown be ominous? He sends all home. Mandodarī’s anxiety deepens from the moment her earrings fell. With tearful eyes and joined hands, she begs her beloved to abandon hostility toward Rāma and not stubbornly regard him as a man. Raghubīra is the cosmic form: every world imagined by the Veda is one of his limbs.",
