    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0015",
      "sequence": 870,
      "meaning": "Mandodarī describes Rāma’s cosmic body: the netherworld is his feet, Brahmā’s realm his head, the other worlds his limbs; Time is the play of his brow, suns his eyes and clouds his hair. The Aśvins are his nostrils; night and day his blinking; directions his ears, wind his breath and Veda his speech. Greed is his lower lip, Yama his terrible teeth, māyā his smile, the guardians his arms; fire his mouth, Varuṇa his tongue, creation, preservation and dissolution his activity. Plants are his hair, mountains bones, rivers veins, oceans belly and hell the lower organs. Śiva is ego, Brahmā intellect, the moon mind and Viṣṇu consciousness. This whole moving and unmoving form dwells as a man. She begs Rāvaṇa to love his feet and preserve her marriage.",
