    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-lanka-kanda-0016",
      "sequence": 871,
      "meaning": "Rāvaṇa laughs at his wife’s words and praises delusion’s force. He repeats a slander that women always hold eight faults—rashness, falsehood, fickleness, illusion, fear, indiscretion, impurity and lack of mercy. He claims she has sung the enemy’s cosmic form merely to frighten him, although everything described lies naturally under his control; thus, he says, she has cleverly proclaimed his own greatness. Her deep speech pleases when understood and removes fear when heard, he jokes. Mandodarī concludes that Time has confused her husband. At dawn proud, fearless Rāvaṇa goes blindly to council; a fool’s heart will not awaken even if Brahmā himself teaches it.",
